-- title:
--   Localised Néron sections embed with finite index into Eisenstein quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \mid \lvert p-1\rvert / \gcd(p-1,12)$, and let $N$ be a datum of type `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent p`: a scheme $G$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ with structure morphism $g$, a relative group law $L$ on $g$, a bijection `N.pts` from $J_0(p) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-sections of $g$, together with commutativity, smoothness, separatedness, finite type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity, connected fibres, additivity and Galois equivariance of `N.pts`, Hecke equivariance, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by $n>0$, and finite index of the subgroup generated by the $\mathbb{Z}$-sections inside the Galois-fixed points. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of abelian groups on the small fppf site of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ (covers by flat, locally finitely presented morphisms) together with bijections $e_U : \mathcal{G}(U) \to \{\varphi : U \to G \mid \varphi \circ g = U \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}\}$ for each fppf object $U$, assumed additive for $L$ and compatible with restriction along each $k : U \to V$. Let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{T} = \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ to $\mathrm{End}(\mathcal{G})$ such that each $t$ is realised by an endomorphism $\varphi$ of $G$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ simultaneously on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points through `N.pts` and on sections through $e$, and let `inst` be a $\mathbb{T}$-module structure on the small copy $M^0 := \mathrm{Shrink}\,H^0_{\mathrm{fppf}}(\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}, \mathcal{G})$ whose action agrees with the maps induced by $\rho$ on cohomology. Then there is an injective additive homomorphism from the localisation of $M^0$ at the complement of the Eisenstein maximal ideal $\mathfrak{P} = (\text{eisensteinEval } p)^{-1}(q)$ into `eisensteinQuotientRationalLocalized p q`, the localisation at the same multiplicative set of the $\mathbb{T}$-span of `eisensteinQuotientRational p`, whose range has finite index.
--
--   This is the comparison, in Mazur's study of the Eisenstein ideal, between the $\mathbb{Z}$-points of the identity component of the Néron model of $J_0(p)$ and the Hecke span of the rational points of the Eisenstein quotient, after localising at the Eisenstein maximal ideal at $q$. It is used in the construction of the primary torsion core attached to $J_0(p)$, namely by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronIdentityComponent.exists_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore_forall_exists_points_embedding`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronIdentityComponent.exists_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore_forall_exists_points_embedding) and [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore_of_dvd).
